---
import DocsLayout from "../../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

import manifestScript from "../../../../examples/worklog/scripts/write-manifest.mjs?raw";

const install = `npm install --save-dev --save-exact @mdbase-dev/connect-dev`;

const cli = `npx mdbase-connect-dev validate-manifest mdbase-app.json
npx mdbase-connect-dev validate-manifest mdbase-app.dev.json --allow-local
npx mdbase-connect-dev validate-contract contracts/example.work-item.json`;

const validate = `import { formatValidationIssues, validateAppManifest } from "@mdbase-dev/connect-dev";

const result = validateAppManifest(manifest, { allowLocal: false });
if (!result.valid) {
  // Each issue has a JSON pointer, such as /requirements/capabilities/required/2.
  console.error(formatValidationIssues(result.issues));
  process.exit(1);
}`;

const pack = `import { defineTypePack } from "@mdbase-dev/connect-dev";

const types = defineTypePack({
  id: "dev.example.worklog",
  version: "1.0.0",
  name: "Worklog",
  resources: [
    {
      kind: "type",
      mode: "seed",
      source: "types/worklog-entry.md",
      target: "_types/worklog-entry.md",
      document: await readFile("mdbase/types/worklog-entry.md", "utf8"),
    },
  ],
});

// In the manifest:
//   "provisions": { "type_packs": [types] }`;

const contract = `import { dataContractDigest, defineDataContract } from "@mdbase-dev/connect-dev";

const workItem = defineDataContract({
  // the contract document; see Contracts and adapters
});

// The digest to put in requirements.contracts and in a type pack's provides.
const digest = dataContractDigest(workItem);`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Developer kit"
  description="@mdbase-dev/connect-dev checks a manifest before you ship it and builds the type packs a manifest carries."
  active="connect-dev"
  headings={[
    { href: "#install", label: "Install" },
    { href: "#cli", label: "Check a manifest" },
    { href: "#build", label: "Check it in a build" },
    { href: "#type-packs", label: "Build a type pack" },
    { href: "#modes", label: "Seed and managed" },
    { href: "#contracts", label: "Contracts" },
    { href: "#script", label: "A whole manifest script" },
    { href: "#sandbox", label: "The sandbox" }
  ]}
>
  <p>
    A build-time package. Nothing from it runs in your app; install it as a
    development dependency.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} language="sh" label="Terminal" />

  <h2 id="cli">Check a manifest</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={cli} language="sh" label="Terminal" />
  <p>
    <code>validate-manifest</code> runs the parser mdbase uses when your app
    registers. It exits non-zero with a list of problems, each with the path
    of the field at fault.
  </p>
  <p>
    An HTTP homepage is refused unless you pass <code>--allow-local</code>.
    Use the flag for a <a href="/sdk/local-development/">development
    manifest</a> and leave it off for the one you publish, so a localhost
    address cannot reach production by mistake.
  </p>

  <h2 id="build">Check it in a build</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={validate} language="js" label="scripts/write-manifest.mjs" />
  <p>
    The SDK also validates the manifest when the app starts. Checking in the
    build moves the failure from your users’ browsers to your own terminal.
  </p>

  <h2 id="type-packs">Build a type pack</h2>
  <p>
    A <a href="/sdk/manifest/#provisioning">type pack</a> carries the type
    and contract files your app adds to a collection. Inside a manifest every
    file is pinned by a SHA-256 digest. <code>defineTypePack()</code> reads
    the documents, computes the digests and returns the object to place under
    {" "}<code>provisions.type_packs</code>:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={pack} language="js" label="scripts/write-manifest.mjs" />
  <table class="api-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Resource field</th>
        <th>Meaning</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>kind</code></td><td><code>"type"</code>, <code>"contract"</code> or <code>"schema"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>mode</code></td><td><code>"seed"</code> or <code>"managed"</code>; see below</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>source</code></td><td>The file’s name inside the pack</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>target</code></td><td>Where it goes in the collection, such as <code>_types/worklog-entry.md</code>. Defaults to <code>source</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>document</code></td><td>The file’s exact text</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>upgradeFrom</code></td><td>Seed types only: earlier versions you shipped, oldest first, that a collection may be upgraded from</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Keep the documents as real files in your repository and read them in the
    script. They are then reviewable in a pull request, and the manifest is a
    build output.
  </p>

  <h2 id="modes">Seed and managed</h2>
  <table class="api-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Mode</th>
        <th>Who owns the file after setup</th>
        <th>Use it for</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>seed</code></td>
        <td>The user. Your app writes it once; later edits by the user stay.</td>
        <td>A type people may want to extend with fields of their own</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>managed</code></td>
        <td>Your app. A new version of your pack updates it.</td>
        <td>A contract, or a type whose exact shape your app depends on</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Adding files to a collection needs the
    {" "}<code>definitions.manage</code> capability in your manifest, and the
    user sees and accepts the change first. See
    {" "}<a href="/sdk/lifecycle/#setup">Setup</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contracts">Contracts</h2>
  <p>
    <code>defineDataContract()</code> validates a
    {" "}<a href="/sdk/contracts/">contract</a> document as you write it, and
    {" "}<code>dataContractDigest()</code> computes the digest a manifest
    names it by.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={contract} language="js" label="contracts.mjs" />
  <p>
    <code>validate-contract</code> on the command line checks a contract file
    the same way.
  </p>

  <h2 id="script">A whole manifest script</h2>
  <p>
    The Worklog example writes its development and deployed manifests from one
    script, validating each:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={manifestScript} language="js" label="scripts/write-manifest.mjs" />

  <h2 id="sandbox">The sandbox</h2>
  <p>
    The package also exports <code>createSandbox()</code>. It is for the
    older <code>@mdbase-dev/connect</code> client. With
    {" "}<code>@mdbase-dev/sdk</code>, test against
    {" "}<code>MemoryReplica</code> and
    {" "}<code>createApplicationFixture()</code>; see
    {" "}<a href="/sdk/testing/">Testing</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
